[17592186507912 #edb/ref 1080 "5\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507912 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507912 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e77d63d4-3768-57eb-87f1-5ab52552457c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507937 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507937 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507937 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa1bd1ce-5d7c-5356-8a41-6149fd10be2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507962 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3915ce74-cbdd-56d7-8c28-9b915fda8173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507979 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "563ab28a-360a-5519-9504-d8c10d6a3bc9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507992 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "71e2b994-15e5-5aeb-82fd-d4bc2277603b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508040 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508040 #edb/ref 1069 "q-1663" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508040 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508040 #edb/ref 1071 "If the hypotenuse of a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle has a length of $2$, then what is the length of each leg?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508040 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0589289f-bd62-59fb-8540-3927d969e746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508040 #edb/ref 1074 "The hypotenuse in a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nHere, we know that the hypotenuse has length $2.$ So, if the length of a leg is $a,$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot a \\\\ a & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the square root from the denominator, we can multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $\\sqrt{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508105 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508105 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82303" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508105 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508105 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/70/70d961102240b0c48132baca8db0b77ed80ff8e0d3b7296bd5c727ab2f97dfd3.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $10+5\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508105 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d933a602-cca3-50d1-9290-6754d9186974" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508105 #edb/ref 1074 "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=10+5\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 10+5\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 5\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 5 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508113 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508113 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508113 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508113 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/27/2788f2795065599063c67d9ae7e9e6ee17cae4aa21198450faf7c09ad10765e1.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $6+3\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508113 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed931f9b-ec89-504b-8f3a-6fc6233992c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508113 #edb/ref 1074 "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=6+3\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 6+3\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 3\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 3 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508143 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186508149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508143 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8730d12c-cd05-5ba6-99b2-4dbdb27838ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508143 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186508113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508149 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a6f7ec19-e013-5d9c-bcfa-d6001e21386c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508149 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186508105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508162 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186508143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508162 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2059ad8-8e80-5bdc-ac88-748ce810f290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508162 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186508040 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
